  "camera_size": 26,
  "note": "午门内、金水桥、太和门 (native:imperial/gate_court, bridges, taihe_gate; 第九章 A): three walled courts in a line behind the 午门's 铁门 — red walls to the sky with dark gold coping, the paving in great worn slabs with dry grass in the joints; the 金水河 green under its five marble bridges (a dragon rail missing claws, moss in the gaps); the bronze lions with their heads rubbed bright; the 太和门's double eaves, faded paint, swallows' nests. Old and used, never tidy: the bloom at the walls' foot, the worn way down the middle.",
